Package: mysterium-vpn
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Mubarak Lawal <mubaraklawal52@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/zamirszn/myst_vpn_linux
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgtk-4-1, systemd, wireguard-tools, nftables, iproute2, ca-certificates, pkexec | policykit-1
Description: Mysterium VPN desktop application
 A native GTK 4 client for Mysterium VPN with a real WireGuard tunnel,
 a kill switch, and automatic reconnection.
 .
 Installing this package adds Mysterium VPN to the application menu. The
 privileged daemon is started at boot and its control socket is given the
 primary group of the desktop user, so no terminal commands, group changes,
 or log-out are required after installation.
